		"comments": [
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " a number abutting the `#`-token before it: the value path keeps the pair as one\n\tword, the media path re-splits it and normalizes the number ",
				"start": 9,
				"end": 155
			},
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " a `#` with no ident content after it heads no token, so the number normalizes on\n\tboth paths ",
				"start": 290,
				"end": 388
			},
			{
				"type": "CSSComment",
				"value": " the same extent decides the hex fold: a colour is a colour only when the token\n\tends at its digits, so a word running on past them is not one ",
				"start": 521,
				"end": 668
			}
		],
		"content": {
			"start": 7,
			"end": 866,
			"styles": "\n\t/* a number abutting the `#`-token before it: the value path keeps the pair as one\n\tword, the media path re-splits it and normalizes the number */\n\t@supports (a: #1.50) and (b: #1.50px) {\n\t\tc {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t@media (a: #1.5) and (b: #1.5px) {\n\t\tc {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t/* a `#` with no ident content after it heads no token, so the number normalizes on\n\tboth paths */\n\t@supports (a: #0.5) and (b: #ABCDE) {\n\t\tc {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t@media (a: #0.5) and (b: #ABCDE) {\n\t\tc {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t/* the same extent decides the hex fold: a colour is a colour only when the token\n\tends at its digits, so a word running on past them is not one */\n\t@supports (a: #FFF.5) and (b: #FFF/5) and (c: #FFFé) and (d: #fff 5) {\n\t\te {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t@media (a: #FFF.5) and (b: #FFF/5) and (c: #FFFé) and (d: #FFF 5) {\n\t\te {\n\t\t\tcolor: red;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n",
			"comment": null
		}
	},
